    "result_text": "Done. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is implemented and all tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1).\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the single place that builds the code. New format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n   - `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the city\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name (unchanged)\n   - `NNNN` = a **per-city** 4-digit sequence = one more than the owners already in that city (previously a global count), computed by filtering `findAll()` on matching city. This step runs before `save`, so the current owner isn't counted.\n   - Updated the Javadoc to match.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 refreshed the `customerCode` description/example and the `membershipNumber` example so the API contract reflects the new format.\n\n**What automatically rebuilt (no code change needed):** the `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper.java` is derived as `owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + YY`, so it now carries the new city-prefixed code (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` now passes against the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` pattern.",
